---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';import {photos} from '../data/photos';import {sources} from '../data/sources';import {places} from '../data/places';
---
<Base title="Sources & photography" description="Trace the photographs, licenses, geographic coordinates and research behind SWAT." section="sources"><header class="page-heading sources-heading"><span class="eyebrow">An open record</span><h1>Every image, a place.<br/>Every claim, a source.</h1><p class="deck">This independent research edition brings together photographs and published accounts. It does not speak on behalf of Swat’s communities.</p></header><div class="sources-layout"><aside class="reading-aside"><nav class="chapter-links"><a href="#photography">Photography & licenses</a><a href="#research">Research & further reading</a><a href="#geography">Geographic data</a><a href="#method">Editorial approach</a></nav></aside><article class="sources-copy"><section id="photography"><h2>Photography</h2><p>All photographs depict identified places in Swat. No generated scenery is used. Images are resized, compressed and cropped for display; some opening images receive a CSS darkening treatment for text contrast. The original files and license terms remain linked below.</p>{photos.map(p=><div class="source-entry" id={`photo-${p.id}`}><Photo id={p.id} detail={false} sizes="(max-width:600px) 90vw,140px"/><h3>{p.title}</h3><p>{p.author} · {p.date}<br/>{p.alt}</p><a href={p.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original photograph ↗</a>{' · '}<a href={p.licenseUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{p.license} ↗</a><p class="caption">Adaptations: responsive crop, compression and display treatment. Adapted photography is offered under the same license as the credited original.</p></div>)}</section><section id="research"><h2>Research & further reading</h2><p><a class="underlink" href="/research/">Search and filter the research index ↗</a></p>{Object.entries(sources).map(([id,s])=><div class="source-entry" id={`source-${id}`}><h3>{s.title}</h3><p>{s.publisher}</p><p>{s.note}</p><a href={s.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the source ↗</a></div>)}</section><section id="geography"><h2>Geography & its limits</h2><p>The atlas uses MapLibre GL JS and OpenFreeMap vector tiles, derived from OpenStreetMap and OpenMapTiles. OpenStreetMap data is licensed under the Open Database License. Place markers use the independently cited coordinates below. The fallback is a coordinate plot, not a terrain or river map.</p><p><a class="underlink" href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">© OpenStreetMap contributors · ODbL ↗</a><br/><a class="underlink" href="https://openfreemap.org/">OpenFreeMap ↗</a> · <a class="underlink" href="https://openmaptiles.org/">OpenMapTiles ↗</a></p>{places.map(p=><div class="source-entry"><h3>{p.name}</h3><p class="source-register">{p.coordinates[1]}° N, {p.coordinates[0]}° E<br/>{p.coordinateMeaning}</p><a href={p.coordinateUrl}>{p.coordinateCredit} ↗</a></div>)}</section><section id="method"><h2>How to read this edition</h2><p>Research and photography describe different moments. Capture dates stay attached to images; publication and sampling dates stay attached to scientific findings. Historical status is stated precisely: UNESCO tentative listing is distinct from inscription.</p><p>The atlas’s lenses interpret documented relationships. They do not claim to draw language boundaries, flood hazard zones or an itinerary. Town markers are representative locations, not navigation instructions or entrances.</p><p>Cultural accounts are attributed to named writers and organisations. No local testimony, archaeological reconstruction, visitor statistic or audio performance has been invented.</p></section></article></div></Base>
